  "title": "Focus on the Quality of an Experience, Not Just Its Duration",
  "description": "Focus on the quality of an experience, not just its duration. Here’s how: - Reflect on highlights: Ask, “What made this moment meaningful?” - Avoid obsessing over length: Long doesn’t always mean better—what mattered most? - Consider the ending: Often, the final moments shape how you remember an experience. Example: A short, joyful trip often leaves a better memory than a long, stressful one.",
